# Cloudflare Pages SPA rewrite.
#
# react-router-dom uses client-side routing, so every path must serve
# index.html or a hard refresh on e.g. /designer/opportunities/:id 404s.
# Same rule netlify.toml already declares for Netlify — Pages reads this
# file from the build output instead, and Vite copies public/ into dist/.
#
# Kept last-resort (200, not 301): it rewrites rather than redirects, so the
# URL the user sees is preserved and the router can read it.
/*    /index.html   200
